## Scope and rules
- Parse only P-family locus records; retain the complete locus ID and tag.
- Allowed P tags: *P0, *Pb, +P0, +P1, +Pb, +Pc, +Pr, =P0, =Pt, @P0, @P1, @Pb.
- Numeric folio IDs and the special identifier fRos are valid.
- Recognize <@H=2> and <@H=3> as local nonstandard annotations, replace each with a token boundary (space), and log exact physical line, locus, marker, and action. Other unknown angle markers fail closed.
- Join physical continuation lines only when the trailing slash and following '/ ' line satisfy the IVTFF continuation rule; malformed/orphan continuations fail closed.
- Remove inline comments.
- Replace standard structural markers <$>, <%>, <->, <~>, and <d> with spaces.
- Preserve text inside curly-brace groups while removing the delimiters.
- Exclude square-bracket alternatives as a whole; do not select a reading.
- Extract ASCII alphabetic sequences and lowercase them.
- Empty cleaned P loci are retained in the audit inventory, not silently discarded.

